{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Operator directive (2026-08-13, supersedes the original debounce idea)\n\"The tickets branch should never trigger CI. The branch is noisy and doesn't contain code.\"\n\n## Findings (measured)\nFour workflows trigger on push to ALL branches, so every rebar write (comment/edit/close auto-push of the tickets branch) fires them: test.yml (full pytest matrix!), verify-identity.yml, optionality.yml, prompt-eval.yml. reconcile-bridge.yml also push-triggers. During the 2026-08-12/13 bug bash this starved GitHub Actions runners (a Verified gate's pytest matrix queued ~2 hours behind tickets-push runs).\n\n## Fix\nExclude the tickets branch from every push trigger (branches-ignore: [tickets] or equivalent explicit branch lists). NO workflow may run on a tickets-branch push.\n\nFunction is retained via existing schedules: reconcile-bridge cron */20 min (worst-case sync latency 20 min), verify-identity 6-hourly, test/optionality 6-hourly, prompt-eval weekly. If reconciliation latency needs to be tighter than 20 min, propose a non-CI mechanism separately - do NOT re-add a push trigger.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] No workflow in .github/workflows/ triggers on a push to the tickets branch (verified by enumerating every on.push trigger).\n- [ ] A tickets-branch push after the change produces zero new workflow runs (observed via the Actions API).\n- [ ] Scheduled coverage for reconcile-bridge and verify-identity is unchanged.\n- [ ] CI-workflow-parity/config gates (test_ci_workflow_parity.py etc.) updated if they pin trigger shapes.\n","title":"Tickets-branch pushes must trigger no CI (operator directive)"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786603834362401001,"uuid":"65bb91ea-2887-4942-8c37-ac273feb0cc2"}